rty":null,"status":"candidate"}]},{"id":"ia-allamakee-waterloo-township-clerk-44","office":"Waterloo Township Clerk","category":"Waterloo Township Clerk","level":"Township","scope":"township","area":"Waterloo","seats":1,"type":"nonpartisan","description":"","cityMaybe":true,"ballotOrder":544,"candidates":[{"name":"David Schulte","party":null,"status":"candidate"}]}],"referendums":[{"id":"ia-amendment-1","name":"Statewide Public Measure 1 — Requirements for Certain State Tax Law Changes","type":"Ratification Of State Constitutional Amendment","statewide":true,"ballotLanguage":"Shall the following amendment to the Constitution be adopted?\n\nProvides that any bill to increase the individual income tax rate or the corporate income tax rate, or the rate of any other type of tax based upon income or legal and special reserves, shall require the affirmative votes of at least two-thirds of the members elected to each house of the legislature for passage. Further, the two-thirds majority vote requirement applies to the passage of a bill to establish a new tax on any type of income or legal and special reserves imposed by the state. The requirement excludes taxes imposed at the option of a local government. A lawsuit challenging the proper enactment of a bill under this section must be filed no later than one year following the enactment.\n\nThe Constitution of the State of Iowa is amended by adding the following new section to new Article XIII: Passage of a bill that increases the individual income tax rate or the corporate income tax rate, or the rate of any other type of tax based upon income or legal and special reserves, shall require the affirmative votes of at least two-thirds of the members elected to each house of the general assembly. This requirement does not apply to taxes imposed at the option of a local government. Passage of a bill that establishes a new tax on any type of income or legal and special reserves imposed by the state shall require the affirmative votes of at least two-thirds of the members elected to each house of the general assembly. A lawsuit challenging the proper enactment of a bill under this section must be filed no later than one year following the enactment. If such a lawsuit is not filed within the one-year limit, the bill shall be considered properly enacted under this section. Each bill to which this section applies must include a separate provision describing the requirements for enactment prescribed by this section. The general assembly shall enact laws to implement this section."},{"id":"ia-retain-john-m-sandy","name":"Retain Court of Appeals Judge John M. Sandy?","type":"Court of Appeals Judge Retention","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"Shall John M. Sandy, Court of Appeals judge, be retained in office? Vote YES to keep the judge or NO to remove the judge."},{"id":"ia-retain-julie-a-schumacher","name":"Retain Court of Appeals Judge Julie A. Schumacher?","type":"Court of Appeals Judge Retention","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"Shall Julie A. Schumacher, Court of Appeals judge, be retained in office? Vote YES to keep the judge or NO to remove the judge."},{"id":"ia-retain-sharon-soorholtz-greer","name":"Retain Court of Appeals Judge Sharon Soorholtz Greer?","type":"Court of Appeals Judge Retention","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"Shall Sharon Soorholtz Greer, Court of Appeals judge, be retained in office? Vote YES to keep the judge or NO to remove the judge."},{"id":"ia-retain-alan-heavens","name":"Retain District Court Judge Alan Heavens? (District 1A)","type":"District Court Judge Retention","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"Shall Alan Heavens, District Court judge (Judicial Election District 1A), be retained in office? Vote YES to keep the judge or NO to remove the judge."},{"id":"ia-retain-mark-t-hostager","name":"Retain District Associate Judge Mark T. Hostager? (District 1A)","type":"District Associate Judge Retention","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"Shall Mark T. Hostager, District Associate judge (Judicial Election District 1A), be retained in office? Vote YES to keep the judge or NO to remove the judge."},{"id":"ia-retain-stephanie-c-rattenborg","name":"Retain District Associate Judge Stephanie C. Rattenborg? (District 1A)","type":"District Associate Judge Retention","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"Shall Stephanie C. Rattenborg, District Associate judge (Judicial Election District 1A), be retained in office? Vote YES to keep the judge or NO to remove the judge."},{"id":"ia-retain-thomas-j-straka","name":"Retain Associate Juvenile Judge Thomas J. Straka? (District 1A)","type":"Associate Juvenile Judge Retention","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"Shall Thomas J. Straka, Associate Juvenile judge (Judicial Election District 1A), be retained in office? Vote YES to keep the judge or NO to remove the judge."},{"id":"ia-allamakee-q-0","name":"Public Measure AM","type":"Local Public Question","statewide":false,"ballotLanguage":"Shall Chapter 22 Library Board of Trustees of the City of Waukon Code of Ordinances be amended as follows: Amending the residency requirements of Trustees, which is currently eight resident members and one nonresident member, to seven resident members, one nonresident member, and one member that could either be a resident or nonresident member, where resident members would continue to be appointed by the City Council with any nonresident members continuing to be appointed by the Allamakee County Board of Supervisors, with Library Trustee terms to be reduced from six (6) years to three (3) years?"}]}